{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar","id":508576,"title":"On the Removal of Unihar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T17:50:39-07:00","id":508576,"title":"On the Removal of Unihar","content":"No, this isn't a complaint thread - though if people want to debate whether or not removing them was the best choice, that's fine - it's simply a query. In the 2e Forsaken corebook, is there anything written that references &quot;yeah, these guys existed, but they don't anymore, not in our canon&quot;? Also, does the corebook at all touch upon what happens when Urathra mates with Urathra? I think I recall hearing somewhere that the result is a wolf-blood of unusual potency, but I can't seem to find the page it's on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:57:56-07:00","id":508595,"title":"","content":"I don't see why they'd need to explicitly state they don't exist anymore, that seems like a waste of word count. And since this isn't oWoD, don't expect the disappearance of a mechanic between editions to have some kind of in-setting justification.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure they're wolf-blooded, and it'll probably be in the Appendix where they're discussed, if anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T22:32:43-07:00","id":508765,"title":"","content":"With the Unihar I honestly could not realistically see a way that werewolf populations could be anywhere near stable. Yes breed with humans or wolf blooded to maybe produce wolf blooded but not all wolf blooded under go the change and what if your wolf blooded mate under goes the change what do you do? I can not give exact page numbers sadly but I believe the child of two urathra is just a wolf blooded mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T23:02:50-07:00","id":508775,"title":"","content":"Nearest thing to mention werewolf-werewolf offspring gets is <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\">in the blog entry from last year</a>, which, as noted, is just fine given that &quot;some measure of werewolf blood&quot; doesn't really need further specification in the absence of unusual cases like the Ghost Children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=508765#post508765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Unihar I honestly could not realistically see a way that werewolf populations could be anywhere near stable. Yes breed with humans or wolf blooded to maybe produce wolf blooded but not all wolf blooded under go the change</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026You do realize the &quot;genetic&quot; point of wolf-blooded in 1e is that they're <i>carriers</i>, right?<br /> <br /> The desirability of incorporating wolf-blooded into one's lineage is that <i>wolf-blooded are more likely to produce children who go on to become werewolves</i>, which do not necessarily register as wolf-blooded prior to the series of events that culminates in the First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T23:11:27-07:00","id":508777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=508595#post508595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they'd need to explicitly state they don't exist anymore, that seems like a waste of word count. And since this isn't oWoD, don't expect the disappearance of a mechanic between editions to have some kind of in-setting justification.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure they're wolf-blooded, and it'll probably be in the Appendix where they're discussed, if anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the cWoD often didn't do that. There was never any explanation for why you no longer needed mirrors to step sideways when Apocalypse went to Revised, no explanation given for the massive changes Fera mechanics often went through between editions or even books that came out less than six months later, not a word about what happened to 2e Vic Stryker's crossover monster pals in Revised, and no explanation for why Renown went from an ever-inflating number to the system of temporary and permanent points. All of them had very good out of character reasons for happening, but as far as the setting was concerned, it was always that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:07:44-07:00","id":508874,"title":"","content":"The word Unihar is not in the book. From what I gathered from the open development post about it, the developers' opinion of the whole thing is &quot;this was a terrible idea, sorry it was ever there, let us never speak of it again.&quot;<br /> I don't remember where it is in the book, but I think there was a side-bar somewhere that offhandedly mentions that some werewolves have old superstitions about Uratha mating, but that they're unfounded and the viewpoint is in the minority. It might be in the section detailing the Oath of the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:31:43-07:00","id":508882,"title":"","content":"We had a lot to cram into the 2e corebook - we couldn't really spend precious space discussing things that <i>weren't</i> in the game any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T12:20:59-07:00","id":509178,"title":"","content":"There are ways to bring them back using existing material. What's to keep an Idigam from producing them? Maybe they arose when a pregnant werewolf was possessed by a Strix and found a way to multiply like Strix do? What might a Maeljin do with a Bale Hound that's become incredibly potent, maybe ascend them into a different form? Maybe the God Machine was getting tired of particular werewolves breaking its infrastructure and created a new type of guard dog? Just change the origin a bit and you can recreate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 05-09-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T12:28:06-07:00","id":509183,"title":"","content":"Making Unihar a new form of Wolf shartha that competes with and preys on the Uratha could work too. Corrupted fragments of Father Wolf perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:18:53-07:00","id":509209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=509183#post509183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Unihar a new form of Wolf shartha that competes with and preys on the Uratha could work too. Corrupted fragments of Father Wolf perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Lodge of Quicksilver Children are onto something. Maybe the children of Father Wolf and Mother Luna were Unihar, and the Idigam they are searching for created the Uratha by using some variation of Forge Servant to stuff them all into the bodies of humans.<br /> <br /> Better yet, maybe Luna <i>is</i> the Idigam. Maybe the Unihar were the Wolf Host fragments of <i>Urfarah</i>, and Luna put them into human bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-09-2015, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:32:29-07:00","id":509218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=508874#post508874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word Unihar is not in the book. From what I gathered from the open development post about it, the developers' opinion of the whole thing is &quot;this was a terrible idea, sorry it was ever there, let us never speak of it again.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Gathered from various sources, I believe it was with the implication of that the woman bares most of the scorn than a father does in Uratha Society. There was also the idea that a the concept of a Unihar (basically a demon baby) conception being used as a weapon via rape was something the devs were off put about.<br /> <br /> Which considering rape as a weapon is legit fear for many women in several countries, I find it odd that the devs put there foot down here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:51:59-07:00","id":509229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=509218#post509218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which considering rape as a weapon is legit fear for many women in several countries, I find it odd that the devs put there foot down here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the fact that &quot;but muh realism&quot; is out of place in a game where shapeshifting berserker demigods walk among the human herd and cull recalcitrant pieces of recurring history, the possibility that you will give birth to an unreasoning miscarriage-nemesis is utterly immaterial to the existence of that tactic\u2026<br /> <br /> The gender divide is kind of a bad thing to base a means of debasement on when your target can turn into a furry engine of destruction, draws on the nominal heritage of at least one being of variable and/or indeterminate gender, and in 2e can indefinitely change which type of equipment they have for a trivial investment of effort.<br /> <br /> 1e's sidebar in The Pure on the subject of sticking Forsaken with unihar pregnancies going out of its way to underline &quot;don't inflict this on a player character without their say-so&quot; doesn't really lend a lot of support to the notion of its necessity even if the FCG's treatment on werewolf romance didn't already lay the groundwork for rolling Ghost Children out the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:33:51-07:00","id":509244,"title":"","content":"From here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ephemera [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The developer saying they removed it from the game.<br /> <br /> 'They have some really unfortunate implications that we want to move away from \u2014 penalising sex with the \u201cwrong\u201d people, casting Wolf-Blooded as breeding stock, punishing female characters far more than male, and a whole mess of problems around their impact on people who have lost pregnancies. I want to stress that nobody on the original design team intended any of this, but a we\u2019re older and wiser we decided to drop a highly problematic element of the game.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:03:18-07:00","id":510085,"title":"","content":"It was because of all the negative implications that I came up with alternate origins, as an opponent they are more than enough to scare unprepared players and it seemed a shame to waste the interesting/useful parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:21:24-07:00","id":510095,"title":"","content":"I just don't know why they went out of their way to keep PCs from having sex with each other. Or at least punish them for doing so. And in such an awful way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:30:35-07:00","id":510101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510095#post510095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't know why they went out of their way to keep PCs from having sex with each other. Or at least punish them for doing so. And in such an awful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that my knowledge of Apocalypse is cursory at best, I'm going to forward the guess that it was a backlash against the prevalence of Metis Garou as a player choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:35:48-07:00","id":510105,"title":"","content":"Metis were stigmatised too. I think it was just another Apocalypse holdover that went a bit overboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:36:41-07:00","id":510107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510101#post510101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that my knowledge of Apocalypse is cursory at best, I'm going to forward the guess that it was a backlash against the prevalence of Metis Garou as a player choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>My knowledge about the matter is about the same, they were meant to be some sort of bad choice but picked a lot, I think. But still, couldn't it just have been solved by making their children wolf-blooded or standard werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2015, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:39:09-07:00","id":510110,"title":"","content":"It was a reaction to Apocalypse, the design team wanted to avoid players walking around in Crinos, only interacting with other werewolves, which was kind of the default behavior in Apocalypse. They intentionally made design decisions to force interaction with normal mortals, and as a side effect lowered the &quot;power level&quot; of the game. I've played Apocalypse more recently than Forsaken and it was that way right off the bat, there was no point in not being in Crinos because we rarely (never) operated around regular humans. Finally getting together players for a 2nd ed game now, have to bribe people to try something new. Part of that bribe is being the guy who's dropping the cash for a copy of Cthulhu Wars this week because it's my birthday next weekend and my folks are sending me some cash. Yaaayyy! I'm such a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 05-10-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:39:10-07:00","id":510111,"title":"","content":"The forbidden romance angle is cool, but I won't cry to see it gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:39:24-07:00","id":510112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510107#post510107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">couldn't it just have been solved by making their children wolf-blooded or standard werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Evidently yes, given that's what happened in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":".  clarifying 05-11-2015, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T03:55:20-07:00","id":510524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=509244#post509244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'They have some really unfortunate implications that we want to move away from \u2014 penalising sex with the \u201cwrong\u201d people, casting Wolf-Blooded as breeding stock, punishing female characters far more than male, and a whole mess of problems around their impact on people who have lost pregnancies. I want to stress that nobody on the original design team intended any of this, but a we\u2019re older and wiser we decided to drop a highly problematic element of the game.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont really care either way about the removal of the Unihar, but that statement stinks of going overboard on the &quot;lets not offend&quot; band wagon. Its a curious desire, to want to make a game where you can rutinely devour other humans merely as sustenance to be more PG.<br /> So brutally murdering a dude and devouring his flesh only to gain back a few points of Essence is fine, but exploring themes of &quot;child birth gone wrong&quot; is a taboo subject? Alright...<br /> <br /> The entire Unihar thing seemed to have a chunk of &quot;teenage comming of age&quot; drama about it, which I never really connected with.<br /> The Unihar were cool, but yeah, I wont really cry to see them gone either and if I did, they would be easy enough to just carry over from 1ed that one could just do that and roll with it unperturbed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:27:45-07:00","id":510536,"title":"","content":"I always felt that unihar were a bit lacking in motive for the whole &quot;come back and murder their parents&quot; thing. I mean, why? I've heard of the terrible twos but that's just ridiculous. <br /> <br /> Maybe they'd work better as vengeful ghost-werewolf things. Not a real ghost, mind you, but maybe when things align just right the resonance of a particularly brutal werewolf death can sort of... coalesce into a werewolf-shaped vengeance spirit thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:59:50-07:00","id":510552,"title":"","content":"I always viewed it as an incest thing. Like, the Werewolfs are all children of Father Wolf so them fucking with each other and having children is just a really grose thing to do. And since this is such an icky thing for them to do, the spirit-abomination thats born of it knows only that its <i>wrong</i> somehow, and that its parents are to blame for that.<br /> So yeah. Incest. Neato. Not really a thematic I really connected with, but if you view as that, it makes a little bit of sense for why they would try to kill they parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:17:20-07:00","id":510559,"title":"","content":"Also incest does not work that way. We're talking so far back that they're as related to each other as people from different countries, potentially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:48:07-07:00","id":510564,"title":"","content":"I know. I didn't say it nessesarily made sense to a human, but the Uratha aren't really human. They're wierd spirit hybirds that might easily obey entirely different 'natural' laws than those we know of. If its been carved into the fabric of the universe by some primordial spirit lord that &quot;All Uratha inbreeding is incest and leads to disaster&quot; then that might simply be how it is.<br /> Its magic. A wizard did it. I aint gotta explain shit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T06:35:35-07:00","id":510572,"title":"","content":"I do not miss the Unihar. Now can Uratha simulate &quot;right&quot; wolf packs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=509218#post509218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which considering rape as a weapon is legit fear for many women in several countries, I find it odd that the devs put there foot down here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rape is also a legit fear for men in several countries (War Rape).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:17:18-07:00","id":510689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510536#post510536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt that unihar were a bit lacking in motive for the whole &quot;come back and murder their parents&quot; thing. I mean, why? I've heard of the terrible twos but that's just ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you are a living abortion, and the ones responsible are still alive.<br /> <br /> Notice, also, that rites and gifts didn't work on them. Why? It's Father Wolf's ban carried over. Since Uratha are only half-spiritual, only their spirit arsenal is nullified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:46:18-07:00","id":510729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510689#post510689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> a living abortion<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure that's an oxymoron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:47:32-07:00","id":510731,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure that's the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:59:06-07:00","id":510747,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it doesn't really work here. What happens is the Unihar is carried to term, &quot;aborts&quot; itself and runs around entirely functional afterwards. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that's called <i>being born.</i> I did that, and I have no particular malice towards my parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:26:52-07:00","id":510770,"title":"","content":"The incest angle never made sense to me in the first place. I'll buy that they're <i>symbolically</i> all family, and since they're part spirit, symbolic incest has more extreme complications than even real incest does for physical beings. But then, shouldn't Wolf-Blooded have produced Unihar too? I guess their symbolic relationship with the Uratha is more like cousins than siblings, but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:33:30-07:00","id":510798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510524#post510524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So brutally murdering a dude and devouring his flesh only to gain back a few points of Essence is fine, but exploring themes of &quot;child birth gone wrong&quot; is a taboo subject? Alright...</div> </div> </div> </div>People in real life are hardly ever getting brutally devoured, but complications with pregnancy is a real and relatively common thing, and invoking the visceral image of it for scares, let alone associating it with punishment and monstrosity is a bit crass.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how one is based on the likely agency of characters and the other revolves around people who probably have the least agency of anybody.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could see a case being made for a World of Darkness game including some ideas where supernatural heritage can cause forms of pregnancy complications and birth defects in terms of &quot;this is a harmful thing that can happen&quot; or &quot;this is something a character might have to grow up with&quot;, but to render it in terms of vengeful monsters is problematic because it cuts too close to stigmatisation of and sense of shame around pregnancy complications and birth defects.<br /> <br /> It would be a bit like watching Game of Thrones and thinking that the perspective that Tyrion Lannister killed his mother was something we were supposed to agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:49:00-07:00","id":510820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510524#post510524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So brutally murdering a dude and devouring his flesh only to gain back a few points of Essence is fine, but exploring themes of &quot;child birth gone wrong&quot; is a taboo subject? Alright...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, eating people for Essence isn't really considered fine. It's against the Oath of the Moon, and a potential Harmony loss. While lots of things alter your harmony, the Oath of the Moon section does suggest that frequent scofflaws should deal with some potentially heavy repercussions.<br /> <br /> I liked the unihar itself, but in the end its just another antagonist, and I'm far more glad werewolves can start having sex with one another.<br /> <br /> You can explore a theme of childbirth gone wrong now. That wasn't the problem with the unihar. The thing with the unihar is <i>all </i>uratha on uratha childbirth going disastrously wrong, but primarily the woman is getting shamed for getting knocked up, even in a non consensual circumstance. Because she broke the Oath of the Moon and had sex with another werewolf. It's just a pretty backwards view for werewolves, who don't seem to hold any gender based views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-11-2015, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:57:58-07:00","id":510999,"title":"","content":"<b>@Levi:</b> Hey! How do you know I wasn't savaged by wolves as a child? I think you're making some pretty hefty assumptions there, mister! ...<br /> Although to be serious, while I can see your point, isn't that precisely why it might be a good idea to allow players to explore those themes? I know I'm referencing a different gameline in the Werewolf forums, but the reason I personally enjoy Promethean so much, is because the theme of being treated unfairly and being ostracised and unable to make friends is something I experienced rather extensively throughout my early to mid teens. I think if I had never experienced that, the main themes of Promethean wouldn't connect that strongly with me.<br /> While I agree that pregnancy gone wrong is a bit more devastating then mere social ostracisation, I still think those themes might resonate all the more strongly with the people who can actually relate those experiences with real life experiences.<br /> <br /> I dont think any book of the WoD ever explicitly stated who you're suposed to root for and fighting against a society that abhors your chosen lifestyle might easily prove for a very entertaining game. This is true in all gamelines. If I suddenly Awakened to a world of magic and god-like supernatural powers, I dont think I would give two shits, when some aged man in a robe came up and told me to stick to the path of Wisdom and obey some obscure set of rules set in latin or ancient greek. I might obey, of a fear of the consequences, but certainly not out of an agreement and all that guy would be saying would besically amount to &quot;Maybe use the toaster when making bread, alright?&quot; and not something as personally offensive as &quot;Dont be with the person you love&quot;.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I dont think its valid to say that just because its a taboo is reason enough to cut it out. I like to think its arts job to help us confront taboo subjects in ways in which we are comfortable, and what situation are you more comfortable than in your own home surrounded by a group of friends large or small?<br /> Now, I personally dont think the Unihar fit all that well into Werewolfs setting as a thematic. I dont think they fit in terribly ill either, but if something isn't great, remove it and try to come up with something which <i>is</i> great, is my general approach, which is why I dont perticularily mind that they've been cut out.<br /> <br /> <b>@nofather:</b> Was it actually ALL Werewolf sex that would result in Unihar? The way I remembered it, it was just a risk that might happen, which - when it did - was terrible enough that all Werewolf-on-Werewolf kink had been strictly forbade. Am I remembering wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:01:55-07:00","id":511002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=510999#post510999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>@nofather:</b> Was it actually ALL Werewolf sex that would result in Unihar? The way I remembered it, it was just a risk that might happen, which - when it did - was terrible enough that all Werewolf-on-Werewolf kink had been strictly forbade. Am I remembering wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, or at least not exactly. Werewolf on werewolf sex didn't always lead to pregnancy, but if it ever did it always led to the unihar. One of the books makes a point of saying the only way to stop it once it has begun is to kill the woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:42:28-07:00","id":511138,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2. Respect the conversation.</span></b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Don\u2019t try to incite others to break the rules, or distract from the subject at hand. This includes threadcrapping, <u>the posting of short messages or images which add nothing to a thread </u>and serve only to express a user\u2019s displeasure with it. Mod edit, Darksider</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 05-11-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:17:47-07:00","id":511208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511138#post511138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing is actually preventing you from exploring whichever themes or antagonists you may use in your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, for that helpful clarification...<br /> If it wasn't immidiately obvious, I wasn't trying to advocate for their return nor was I crying that they had been removed. I was merely discussing the topic of their removal in a slightly more broad manner than simply going &quot;I think it sucks!&quot; or &quot;I think its gud!&quot;.<br /> And yes. That was merely my opinion. Another opinion that I also seem to be alone in keeping, is the radical idea that its possible to express disapproval of a persons opinion or conduct in a manner that doesn't make oneself come off like a smarmy twit in the process.<br /> Although such opinions are unrelated to any discussion that might be going on in a roleplay forum...Or atleast so they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:34:38-07:00","id":511242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">isn't that precisely why it might be a good idea to allow players to explore those themes?</div> </div> </div> </div> In the form of vengeful, murderous ghost babies who come for you for daring to become pregnant with somebody you weren't socially permitted to? No. As a general thing? Still no. If individuals have a need for that personally, I wish them all luck, but to make a hefty portion of the game about it? That smacks me of appropriation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:00:44-07:00","id":511273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511242#post511242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the form of vengeful, murderous ghost babies who come for you for daring to become pregnant with somebody you weren't socially permitted to? No. As a general thing? Still no. If individuals have a need for that personally, I wish them all luck, but to make a hefty portion of the game about it? That smacks me of appropriation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might just be my memory that isn't as well excercised in this regard as I assumed it was, but to my memory, they were never really &quot;a hefty portion of the game&quot;.<br /> The general impression I've gotten off of Werewolf, isn't that its about love dramas and sensual play (which, honestly, is a point very much in favor of removing the Unihar), so they're only really there if anyone wants to explore those themes in the first place. Otherwise, the characers just dont have sex with other Werewolfs, and it doesn't come up.<br /> Its kinda like saying that keeping your magical practises a secret from your familly is a hefty part of Awakening. Thats true, if a player decides to have a familly.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I still kinda fail to see why you think its such a big deal and taboo subject. In my opinion, the most interesting stories spring from the issues that mirror our current social issues or certain issues that are timeless, like greed, war or love. Thats whats so neat about stories and roleplay in particular. It lets us engage in certain activities and experiences which we would find terrible if they happened in reality and construct scenarioes that lets us mirror real world issues in funny ways. I imagine that in Werewolf 1ed society, it would be alright for a pair of Werewolfs to be gay, since no pregnancy is going to come of that. So in effect, the Unihar causes the Uratha society to mirror our own society, but it flips it around. Whats socially acceptable to us is terribly forbidden for them and whats kinda socially stigmatized for us are alright for them.<br /> Oh, by the way, I feel like I need to ask if this kind of meta-discussion is too tangential to the actual subject of the thread? I think its interesting to have this discussion, but if its too off topic, I'll stop prolonging this particular discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:46:20-07:00","id":511304,"title":"","content":"This debate seems semi-moot to me. Its not like the developers designed anything so that unihar are impossible to add to the setting again. I like the idea of the unihar and ill be keeping them in my stories. I don't think there exists a single rule in second edition or setting detail that now conflicts with this. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T18:53:38-07:00","id":511407,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 there's the matter of coming up with a different cause behind the unihar, since 2e has clearly stated that two werewolves mating results in a wolf-blooded or an ordinary mortal, just like werewolf/mortal matings. But once you've got a justification for why they exist, there's no problem with including them in your game. <br /> <br /> Heck, if you want to reintroduce the \u201cunihar are the result of two werewolves mating\u201d thing, Onyx Path isn't going to break down your door and confiscate your books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:06:47-07:00","id":511410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511407#post511407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well\u2026 there's the matter of coming up with a different cause behind the unihar, since 2e has clearly stated that two werewolves mating results in a wolf-blooded or an ordinary mortal, just like werewolf/mortal matings. But once you've got a justification for why they exist, there's no problem with including them in your game.<br /> <br /> Heck, if you want to reintroduce the \u201cunihar are the result of two werewolves mating\u201d thing, Onyx Path isn't going to break down your door and confiscate your books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm adding my voice to this chorus: if you change the origins of Unihar, you can get a formidable and interesting antagonist for the pack. I'm drawing a blank on those alternate origins right now, but I'll be sure to post here when I've thought of a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:07:32-07:00","id":511412,"title":"","content":"I could see, for example, the unihar as the result of two werewolves with harmony way way into the spirit side of things so that they give birth to a spirit, and considering the innately cannibalistic nature of spirits in nwod it's not like that is likely to go well.<br /> <br /> Although now that I think about it, the unihar, even seen through the lense of spirit behavior, is rather extreme.<br /> <br /> Sure, tree spirits eat other tree spirits, among other things, but I doubt many tree spirits feel a burning passion to kill off all other tree spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:11:34-07:00","id":511414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511412#post511412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could see, for example, the unihar as the result of two werewolves with harmony way way into the spirit side of things so that they give birth to a spirit, and considering the innately cannibalistic nature of spirits in nwod it's not like that is likely to go well.<br /> <br /> Although now that I think about it, the unihar, even seen through the lense of spirit behavior, is rather extreme.<br /> <br /> Sure, tree spirits eat other tree spirits, among other things, but I doubt many tree spirits feel a burning passion to kill off all other tree spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're more like particularly violent ghosts, really \u2014 their driving impetus is the cessation of the things that brought them into existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:19:23-07:00","id":511416,"title":"","content":"<i>Blood of the Wolf</i>, the book I like least in first edition, explained in great detail how certain shapeshifting could kill the unborn child of a werewolf.<br /> <br /> One of the rumors it suggested was that the crushed soul of an unborn child could become a sort of proto-<i>unihar</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T20:45:32-07:00","id":511564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511410#post511410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm adding my voice to this chorus: if you change the origins of Unihar, you can get a formidable and interesting antagonist for the pack. I'm drawing a blank on those alternate origins right now, but I'll be sure to post here when I've thought of a good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>First page of this thread has more than a few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:13:22-07:00","id":511674,"title":"","content":"On the thematic appropriateness of the unihar in the setting: <br /> <br /> &quot;What is our ban, boy?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ban? But... I thought only spirits got those!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh but we are half spirit ourselves... Like Father Wolf before us, we cannot defend ourselves from our murderous offspring. Since we aren't fully spirit, and bans are spiritual things, this applies to our gifts and rites. Thus why our gifts don't work on our offspring.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Two people mate, the resulting offspring receives one randomly chosen gene from each of its parents' gene pair. What you get is still based on the genes of the mother and the father.<br /> <br /> Two werewolves mate, the resulting offspring is 500 pounds of raging wolf-death with an unstoppable thirst for genocide. <br /> <br /> Lycanthropy is recessive. Every living werewolf bears human blood (lots of it) in addition to what little is left of Father Wolf's lifeblood. With every continuing generation, Father Wolf's bloodline is further diluted.<br /> <br /> Now, if two werewolves mate, what they should produce is a child with a lot more of Father Wolf's blood than what's common these days, right? Instead .. we all know know what happens.<br /> <br /> Makes you think about the nature of lycantrophy and of Father Wolf, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T00:56:29-07:00","id":511785,"title":"","content":"I am very pleased that Onyx Path removed Unihar and its implications from the canon rules.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T21:19:43-07:00","id":512514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511674#post511674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lycanthropy is recessive. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that it's useful to think of mystical bloodlines in the manner of really simplistic genetic models. One involves a single protein that's basically been switched off and lost its normal function, the other turns you into a shapeshifting demigod. Not a really close comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T21:33:24-07:00","id":512516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511674#post511674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the thematic appropriateness of the unihar in the setting:<br /> <br /> &quot;What is our ban, boy?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ban? But... I thought only spirits got those!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh but we are half spirit ourselves... Like Father Wolf before us, we cannot defend ourselves from our murderous offspring. Since we aren't fully spirit, and bans are spiritual things, this applies to our gifts and rites. Thus why our gifts don't work on our offspring.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Two people mate, the resulting offspring receives one randomly chosen gene from each of its parents' gene pair. What you get is still based on the genes of the mother and the father.<br /> <br /> Two werewolves mate, the resulting offspring is 500 pounds of raging wolf-death with an unstoppable thirst for genocide.<br /> <br /> Lycanthropy is recessive. Every living werewolf bears human blood (lots of it) in addition to what little is left of Father Wolf's lifeblood. With every continuing generation, Father Wolf's bloodline is further diluted.<br /> <br /> Now, if two werewolves mate, what they should produce is a child with a lot more of Father Wolf's blood than what's common these days, right? Instead .. we all know know what happens.<br /> <br /> Makes you think about the nature of lycantrophy and of Father Wolf, doesn't it?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for articulating the other part of why Unihar were a cancer that needed to be removed.<br /> <br /> I. Hate. Diluted. Bloodline. Of. Awesome. It brings up the specter of (urgh) breeding programs and eugenics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T23:19:46-07:00","id":512631,"title":"","content":"Good news, then. If you\u2019re wolf-blooded, you can potentially become a werewolf; and an <i>ordinary mortal</i> can become wolf-blooded in 2e: all she needs to do is to Dramatically Fail to resist Lunacy. No heritage is required. <br /> <br /> Of course, that replaces eugenics and breeding programs with torturing mortals until they crack, and then hoping they\u2019ll be your friends; so it's not much of an improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T02:41:57-07:00","id":512754,"title":"","content":"The Ivory Claws will probably still practice those eugenics and breeding programs, but as they are antagonists that is to be expected. But nothing rules out that some packs of Forsaken might also be convinced that it is mostly a matter of breeding. It is not like there are scientific studies that test how people become werewolves to dispell that notion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:42:58-07:00","id":512951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=512514#post512514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that it's useful to think of mystical bloodlines in the manner of really simplistic genetic models. One involves a single protein that's basically been switched off and lost its normal function, the other turns you into a shapeshifting demigod. Not a really close comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>It behaves like it, regardless, I seriously doubt science in the WoD would be able to isolate the &quot;shapeshifter&quot; gene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:44:09-07:00","id":512953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=512631#post512631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news, then. If you\u2019re wolf-blooded, you can potentially become a werewolf; and an <i>ordinary mortal</i> can become wolf-blooded in 2e: all she needs to do is to Dramatically Fail to resist Lunacy. No heritage is required.<br /> <br /> Of course, that replaces eugenics and breeding programs with torturing mortals until they crack, and then hoping they\u2019ll be your friends; so it's not much of an improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Stockholm Syndrome. Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:14:51-07:00","id":513217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=511273#post511273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be my memory that isn't as well excercised in this regard as I assumed it was, but to my memory, they were never really &quot;a hefty portion of the game&quot;.<br /> The general impression I've gotten off of Werewolf, isn't that its about love dramas and sensual play (which, honestly, is a point very much in favor of removing the Unihar), so they're only really there if anyone wants to explore those themes in the first place. Otherwise, the characers just dont have sex with other Werewolfs, and it doesn't come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really didn't expect this thread to go beyond the yes/no answer it seemed to have asked for. Since it has, though, it's been on my mind a lot.<br /> My wife miscarried our first child. Given that we were both really excited to have kids, this was a really really traumatic experience for us. It's not something I'm chomping at the bit to role-play an extreme version of.<br /> Now, I get the whole &quot;lets play out the hard things in life&quot; idea. It makes sense from certain perspectives and can make for some excellent drama. And facing the things that have been hard in your life can be therapeutic.<br /> Here's the problem with the Unihar, though. You're right; they weren't a big part of the game. You give someone the 1-minute sell (or probably even the half-hour sell) on the game, and you're not going to say &quot;oh and by the way you can't mate with other Werewolves in this game because it'll make a murdering rage beast that will come and kill you both. And the only way to stop it early is to kill the mother. Even it she was a rape victim&quot;. <br /> Now the reason that's the problem with them is that the issues this dredges up are also not surface issues. If you know a rape victim, you don't necessarily know that you know a rape victim. I've been on this forum for several months now and posted several hundred times and I don't think anyone else here knew I had been personally touched by a problem pregnancy.<br /> You add those two hidden things together and you get bombs. Werewolf is a cool game where you get to tap the things that go bump in the night on the shoulder and then murder them. There's a lot of apeal to that. But to implant it with this weird sub-theme where if you want to play it and your character does have a relationship with another werewolf, a good pregnancy will never come to pass leads to emotionally dangerous territory.<br /> And Werewolf is supposed to be a sensual game. Wolf senses are hyper-driven, and that's called out a lot, so it should lead to emotionally heady, visceral stories. To make all of those stories lead to &quot;your children will not be your children and you must be killed for being pregnant&quot; isn't good.<br /> <br /> They added lots of better options in the 2nd edition book. There's a whole section on dealing with pregnancy, including persistent Conditions for the various trimesters. They make specific mention that, given the supernatural nature of the setting, male characters can get pregnant if they want to. They specifically say to Storytellers &quot;don't put the baby in real jeapordy unless your players want to play that story. Let the player keep playing their character.&quot;<br /> This all goes a long way towards living up to the &quot;Don't Say No&quot; storytelling component. As interesting an antagonist as the Unihar might be, their creation at every Werewolf-on-Werewolf pregnancy did more to quash story lines than it did to make new ones. And in a very player-violent way.<br /> <br /> I am very much behind the developers' decisions and statements regarding them. And I'm all for the people in this thread putting them back in for their various different reasons and with their various new origins. If you're leaving in their original origin, though, tell your players ahead of time and get their sign-off. Don't kill children just because its the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T13:25:10-07:00","id":513262,"title":"","content":"Have I mentioned that my single biggest suggestion when bringing back the Unihar is to <i>not</i> tie them to werewolves mating with other werewolves? \u201cWerewolves must not mate with werewolves\u201d is a holdover from WtA, and should be left there, the way WtF1e took pains to exclude werewolves mating with wolves from the game. <br /> <br /> Indeed, if you want to tie Unihar to forbidden mating in 2e, I'd recommend tying them to bestiality instead of same-species mating. That keeps the original intent of \u201cthe werewolf conducted a forbidden mating, and the result is a Ghost Child\u201d while removing the unfortunate implications of it being a bad thing to mate with someone who is your equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-13-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:26:05-07:00","id":513438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=513262#post513262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I mentioned that my single biggest suggestion when bringing back the Unihar is to <i>not</i> tie them to werewolves mating with other werewolves? \u201cWerewolves must not mate with werewolves\u201d is a holdover from WtA, and should be left there, the way WtF1e took pains to exclude werewolves mating with wolves from the game.<br /> <br /> Indeed, if you want to tie Unihar to forbidden mating in 2e, I'd recommend tying them to bestiality instead of same-species mating. That keeps the original intent of \u201cthe werewolf conducted a forbidden mating, and the result is a Ghost Child\u201d while removing the unfortunate implications of it being a bad thing to mate with someone who is your equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but killing a pregnant animal is considerably less morally damning than considering doing the same with a person. Now, mating with actual spirits, or Claimed, or someone influenced by a particularly nasty sort of Wounded spirit, on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:27:33-07:00","id":513446,"title":"","content":"There is a shaman in the fiction who is rumored to have sex with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:49:38-07:00","id":514064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar?p=513446#post513446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a shaman in the fiction who is rumored to have sex with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And men can carry offspring to life.<br /> <br /> WtF 2e is no longer spirit-police.<br /> And actually letting humans and spirits breed potential wolfblooded offspring is a great narraative for a character or a potential pack member.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}